From abce52ff8e3151b72ed32b46be38101955300c79 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Micheal Waltz <micheal@ecliptik.com>
Date: Mon, 6 Jul 2026 11:51:01 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] patch 0263 -- fix fmt format strings that crash DJGPP at
 runtime

Two LOG_* calls used format strings that fmt cannot process, and on
this build that is fatal rather than cosmetic.

The DOS build bundles fmt 12.1.0 but is pinned to C++11 (see
0002-cmake-djgpp-target-flags.patch). fmt's consteval compile-time
format-string checking requires C++20, so under C++11 fmt falls back to
RUNTIME format parsing. An uncaught fmt::format_error is std::terminate
on DJGPP -- i.e. an instant quit-to-DOS with no orderly shutdown. This
is the exact failure class that produced bug #38 (fixed in 0258); these
are two more instances of it that static review surfaced.

  * src/tsc.cpp:1391 -- LOG_WARN mixed a printf "%s" (which fmt treats
    as literal text) with a real field "{:#04d}". fmt bound the FIRST
    argument -- cmd_table[cmd].mnemonic, a const char* -- to the integer
    presentation "d", which throws format_error. This LOG_WARN sits at
    WARN level (>= the default INFO threshold) so it ALWAYS formats when
    reached. Trigger: a TSC script executes an opcode that is a known
    mnemonic but unimplemented in the switch (cmd < OP_COUNT). The
    intended behavior is a graceful "script halted" warning; instead the
    engine terminated to DOS. Stock Cave Story data does not hit this,
    but third-party mods / future opcodes do. Fixed by replacing "%s"
    with "{}", matching the already-correct sibling call at tsc.cpp:1395.

  * src/map.cpp:1732 -- LOG_DEBUG used "{:%02d}", which is not valid fmt
    replacement-field grammar ('%' is not a legal fill/align/type), so
    fmt throws format_error while parsing the field. This is DEBUG level
    and the DJGPP logger short-circuits below the default INFO threshold
    before formatting, so it is latent today -- but it becomes a hard
    crash the moment anyone raises the log level (e.g. to diagnose an
    unrelated issue) and an object appears on a flag. Fixed to "{:02d}".

Both are pure log-string corrections: placeholder count now equals
argument count and every field's presentation type matches its argument
type. No behavior change on any non-crashing path; no new hint, killswitch,
or banner.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Code <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/map.cpp | 2 +-
 src/tsc.cpp | 2 +-
 2 files changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/map.cpp b/src/map.cpp
index 355ed9ab..1de7701b 100644
--- a/src/map.cpp
+++ b/src/map.cpp
@@ -1729,7 +1729,7 @@ bool load_entities(const std::string &fname)
         if (game.flags[id1])
         {
           addobject = true;
-          LOG_DEBUG("Appearing object {:%02d} ({}) because flag {} is set", id2, DescribeObjectType(type), id1);
+          LOG_DEBUG("Appearing object {:02d} ({}) because flag {} is set", id2, DescribeObjectType(type), id1);
         }
       }
       else if (flags & FLAG_DISAPPEAR_ON_FLAGID)
diff --git a/src/tsc.cpp b/src/tsc.cpp
index f9ae6c43..b1b2341d 100644
--- a/src/tsc.cpp
+++ b/src/tsc.cpp
@@ -1388,7 +1388,7 @@ void TSC::ExecScript(ScriptInstance *s)
       {
         if (cmd < OP_COUNT)
         {
-          LOG_WARN("- unimplemented opcode %s; script #{:#04d} halted.", cmd_table[cmd].mnemonic, s->scriptno);
+          LOG_WARN("- unimplemented opcode {}; script #{:#04d} halted.", cmd_table[cmd].mnemonic, s->scriptno);
         }
         else
         {
